{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_111","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport requests,re\nhtml=requests.get('https://eyemultiome.su.domains/retina.html',timeout=30).text\nprint(html)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n\t<title>Eye Multiome</title>\n\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n\t<link href=\"https://maxcdn.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.5.2/css/bootstrap.min.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\t<style type=\"text/css\">td {\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\t</style>\n<style class=\"jodit jodit-table-container jodit-box jodit_theme_default\">html:nth-of-type(1) > body:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-of-type(1) > table:nth-of-type(2) > tbody:nth-of-type(1) > tr:nth-of-type(1) > td:nth-of-type(1){border: 1px double #1e88e5 !important;}</style></head>\n<body style=\"direction: ltr; min-height: 901px;\" dir=\"ltr\" spellcheck=\"false\">\n<div class=\"container-fluid\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<nav class=\"col-sm-3 col-md-2\" id=\"sidebarMenu\">\n<ul class=\"nav flex-column\">\n\t<li class=\"nav-item\">\n\t<h5><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#abstract\">Abstract</a></span></h5>\n\t</li>\n\t<li class=\"nav-item\">\n\t<h5><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#explore\">Explore</a></span></h5>\n\t</li>\n\t<li class=\"nav-item\">\n\t<h5><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#data\">Data</a></span></h5>\n\t</li>\n\t<li class=\"nav-item\">\n\t<h5><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#citation\">Citation</a></span></h5>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n</nav>\n\n<div class=\"col-sm-9 col-sm-offset-3 col-md-10 col-md-offset-2 main\">\n<div class=\"page-header\">\n<h1><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Single-cell multiome of the human retina and deep learning nominate causal variants in complex eye diseases</span></h1>\n</div>\n\n<hr>\n<h4><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Abstract</span></h4>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) of eye disorders have identified hundreds of genetic variants associated with ocular disease. However, the vast majority of these variants are noncoding, making it challenging to interpret their function. Here, we present a joint single-cell atlas of gene expression and chromatin accessibility of the adult human retina with &gt;50,000 cells, which we used to analyze single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) implicated by GWAS of age-related macular degeneration, glaucoma, diabetic retinopathy, myopia, and type 2 macular telangiectasia. We integrate this atlas with a HiChIP enhancer connectome, expression quantitative trait loci (eQTL) data, and base-resolution deep learning models to predict noncoding SNPs with causal roles in eye disease, assess SNP impact on transcription factor binding, and define their known and novel target genes. Our efforts nominate pathogenic SNP-target gene interactions for multiple vision disorders and provide a potentially powerful resource for interpreting noncoding variation in the eye.</span></span></p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Explore</span></h4>\n\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; border: 1px solid rgb(221, 221, 221);\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(221, 221, 221); padding: 8px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Cell-type gene expression browser</span></strong></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(221, 221, 221); padding: 8px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Single Cell Portal UMAP</span></strong></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(221, 221, 221); padding: 8px;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Chromatin accessibility tracks<br>\n\t\t\tand H3K27ac HiChIP loops</span></strong></td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(221, 221, 221); padding: 8px;\"><a href=\"https://eyemultiome.shinyapps.io/humanretinascrna/\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><img alt=\"Gene expression browser\" src=\"/images/scRNADotPlotIcon.png\" style=\"border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; width: 400px; height: 615px;\"></span></a></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(221, 221, 221); padding: 8px;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https://singlecell.broadinstitute.org/single_cell/study/SCP1755/joint-scrna-seq-and-scatac-seq-atlas-of-the-adult-human-retina\"><img alt=\"scRNA UMAP\" src=\"/images/scRNAUMAPIcon.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 615px; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid;\"></a></span></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(221, 221, 221); padding: 8px;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https://epigenomegateway.wustl.edu/browser2022/?blob=7Zpbj9o4FMe_CkofS0LCZQZ4o6gXtJ1pNbDdh1VVOc4h8Y6xU8cMZUbz3XscQgiQ0ukyiio18ILjv.1z.eVgTB6sEIRcwDVZgDW0orDTt5rWHYPVRGhQd4Rbwwcr0URpa9gedLuDy3a_M2haIIL0Qu.i2_c6g8empRWht4k1_PfBEpvZbpYcFE6n17FpqqzJiQ84bd4tY82kwJEPB1046VKZJooWoElANDGqmVmpsTcrSlkyBQ5UAxo2JzyBpjVnHD74_21mMA1j3ueCqfiZJTP4hs5lQzQ2xlLMWYgr4awkZsXm1yWo9WsRxJIJHPTw.NjcuQsxEH1Fkts9r9Ori.3V3MN9cVkMioo8FJHWcTJste7YfbT0ndUy0dyBYNmKlz5ntGUy2FKL5Na7cHz_ZOCKhv0O8VMwfwsCdqFDNIEIITUxwdkL3nwKXxumP8ksKwwZFYeUBrYw.kmMHRmyuWm2N8xvAZ8MdoHzWbjCQYWApb1lsUg7qORSYeuF511edjp4BUQCC59P9ZrjhKl5RwjSiIjQ3nBnm7g5ScdZJvYKEm17DlmQeynIKnGoXLSmGMDWDWgmyMurJUdDFvAyoaPZaPwyVjKNTwutsWf4acruwfZc1xZSLa5AR3j9BkiQTMRsOrVHikY3jr86SNl.Upr7KcxC8v9TlQY_XwJ1Z.YujeZrpdLAm9SZtUZBUDAryeycEX8iAvhmDd2mZbzFOx8HjfHel4tGOhAdy1H48OaNTaWAhs9iyUmhFh1xUSItgaRElRPT7RIyGBzXp.eHA61AsQAns6Im5WxSMNb45dkIO